{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ALL REMAINING ACs NOW HAVE CHANGES UP FOR REVIEW. Stack: 1584 -> 1585 -> 1588.\n\n1588 — 'rebar tracker-maintenance', the supported door (ACs 6, 7, 8):\n  * BACKUP REF BEFORE THE FIRST WRITE — refs/rebar-maintenance/<utc> at current HEAD,\n    printed with its rollback command. Tested: the ref must point at HEAD-BEFORE, not after.\n  * REFUSAL on unpushed ticket commits (rev-list origin/tickets..HEAD non-empty). A refused\n    run makes NO writes AT ALL, backup ref included — that is asserted, not assumed. It fails\n    CLOSED: a missing origin/tickets also refuses, because local commits cannot then be proven\n    safe. Treating 'unknowable' as zero would defeat the guard.\n  * DURABLE AUDIT — actor (git identity, falling back to $USER), argv, backup ref,\n    unpushed count, forced flag + reason, and the paths touched; appended as JSONL to the\n    tracker's GIT DIR, deliberately not the worktree, so it can never become store content a\n    later merge conflicts on.\n  * BREAK-GLASS --force=<reason>: requires a written reason (bare --force is rejected exit 2),\n    loud on stderr, recorded as forced:true with the reason.\n  * DOCS state the rule and name the break-glass: AGENTS.md pointer, a new\n    docs/concurrency.md section 'Mutating the tracker: no AD-HOC raw git', cli-reference.md\n    (generated), exit-codes.md.\n6 envelope tests cover the above.\n\nDESIGN NOTE: the foreign-path classifier is single-sourced as fsck.foreign_store_path_list —\nfsck renders it, tracker-maintenance ACTS on it. Two copies would be free to drift, and a\nrepair that disagreed with the report it was shown could delete something fsck never named.\n\nCI FOUND TWO THINGS MY LOCAL RUN DID NOT — both real, both fixed:\n  1. raw-git-write gate: its '# raw-git-ok:' marker is keyed to the CALL's own line, so\n     markers placed on the preceding comment line do not count. Affected the new\n     reset --hard / update-ref / rm calls. Fixed by moving each call onto its own line with\n     the marker attached.\n  2. docs/cli-reference.md is GENERATED; I had hand-edited it. Regenerated with\n     scripts/gen_cli_reference.py, which produces a better entry than mine (it inlines the\n     full help text including the safety envelope). All four generators now pass --check.\n\nGATE STATUS: 1584 is LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1. 1585 LLM +1, CI running. 1588 re-pushed,\ngates running. Ticket stays OPEN until the stack merges."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786384276451390001,"uuid":"3e3fdb5f-8320-4aa9-bc1d-10429eda13cf"}